    simili: ["altri-lavori","ingresso-onore-fiera-pesaro","motomuseo-morbidelli"],
    en: {"titolo":"Design and signage","luogo":"Pesaro","tag":["Signage","Design","Lighting"],"intervento":"Lighting research, urban and corporate signage, furniture components","progettisti":["With the architects Massimo D’Agnillo and Andrea Pagnetti, renderings Studio Luca Bartolini","BIESSE totem: with Studio Skooter and the architect Carmelo Grasso"],"testo":"<p>In 1987-88 I carried out an in-depth market study on outdoor lighting systems for public and private spaces for Frank Soriano and Surya Illuminazione of Montecatini Terme, travelling across Italy to investigate the most advanced methods and technologies. The research became the brief on which the Tuscan company invited internationally renowned architects and designers — Francesco Cellini, Adolfo Natalini, Umberto Riva, Pierluigi Nicolin, Enzo Mari, Piero Menichetti, Juan Navarro Baldeweg, Santiago Calatrava — to design. I stayed in close touch with them for a time, especially with Enzo Mari, visiting his studio in Piazzale Baracca in Milan several times.</p><p>Design of bathroom fittings and accessories for people with disabilities, with the Pesaro branch of the Italian Spastic Care Association, for the International Ideas Competition on accessible bathrooms promoted by Centro Studi OIKOS: the project received a special mention and was published in “Bagno & Accessori”, September-October 1988, no. 111.</p><ul><li>Signage for the historic centre: Municipality of Pesaro, Department of Commerce, with the architects Massimo D’Agnillo and Andrea Pagnetti, renderings by Studio Luca Bartolini</li><li>“Il Motocida”: a barrier keeping motorbikes out of public green spaces, with Michele Gambini, then district council president</li><li>Design study for a balcony railing, renderings by the architect Andrea Pagnetti</li><li>Study for a signage kiosk for Pesaro’s seafront: model</li><li>BIESSE S.p.A. totem: design and production of the corporate signage totem installed at every site of the industrial group, which makes machinery for working wood, marble and glass; with Studio Skooter Pesaro, the architect Carmelo Grasso, renderings by Studio Luca Bartolini</li><li>Stained-glass chandelier for a library in Tripoli (Libya): commissioned to Pesaro Vetrate, I conceived and drew the construction design of the 10×10-metre, 2.5-metre-high structure — five concentric rings in an inverted cone, weighing 2.5 tonnes of iron and 2.5 of glass; structural design by Studio Tecos, engineer Michele Ranocchi</li></ul>"},
